{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "15eed9d8-6d5a-8a4c-9fbf-cb4cd8f3630f",
  "created_at": "2025-12-02T11:29:08-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Margaret Gifford",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:26:29-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:26:33-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi Tony. Well, if it isn't the one person in Newport who answers on the second ring. Look, I'm calling about my water bill and it's got to be wrong."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:26:44-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ha, I'll take it. Okay, what's going on with it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:26:48-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's way up. Like, double what I normally pay. And I was out of town for six weeks. Nobody was in the apartment. So the usage shouldn't be high at all."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:27:00-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Gotcha. Can I get the service address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:27:03-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "437 Bacheller Street. Margaret Gifford. I rent, but the bill comes to me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:27:08-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, Ms. Gifford, give me one second. [pause] Yep, I see it. The reading is a lot higher than your usual quarter. So the meter shows water going through even while you were away."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:27:21-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's what I don't get. Unless, hold on, the toilet. It was running constantly last month, before I left. I jiggled the handle, it'd stop, then start again. I told the landlord, but I don't know if anyone came."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:27:35-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That could do it, honestly. A running toilet can use a lot of water over six weeks, and the meter just counts whatever passes through. A good test is a few drops of food coloring in the tank. If it shows up in the bowl without flushing, it's leaking."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:27:53-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so it's probably my own toilet. Great. Fantastic. Can the bill be adjusted at all?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:28:00-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can note the account and have someone look at whether a leak adjustment applies once it's repaired. I'd get the toilet fixed first and keep the receipt or the landlord's note."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:28:12-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fine. I'll push the landlord. Now, how do I pay it? I work days, I'm out of the house by seven and not back until after five. Can I pay in person after 4:30, or in the evening somewhere?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:28:26-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Counter closes before that, unfortunately. But there's a drop box at City Hall you can use anytime with a check, and you can pay online or by phone with a card whenever it's convenient, even at night."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:28:40-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Online's fine, I'll do that tonight. Sorry, I can barely hear you, there's a doorbell going off. [crosstalk] The neighbor across the street just got this very loud new doorbell. It sounds like a church bell every time the mail comes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:28:55-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Ha, that'll keep you on your toes. Anything else on the account?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:29:00-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No, that's it. Thanks, Tony."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-02T11:29:03-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome. I'll put the note on there. Have a good one."
    }
  ],
